  "slug": "functional-antigens-08fc",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications release reproducible workflows and annotation resources for human variant analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational infrastructure for interpreting human genomic variation, spanning read processing, variant calling, haplotype phasing and functional annotation. Several items emphasize reproducibility and performance. MitoArc packages a Nextflow workflow for short-read mtDNA analysis with explicit NUMT evidence and benchmarks on synthetic truth data, while BRISANCE reports a 20.6-fold speedup for somatic SNV and indel calling from tumor-normal WGS when compared against DRAGEN. vep-rs reimplements Ensembl VEP in Rust, reporting up to 440-fold faster annotation with documented divergences. Other items focus on annotation content: hlafactor integrates HLA functional annotations such as tapasin dependency and NK ligand groups, and MissenseDB combines three transformer missense predictors with structural and ClinVar context. Phirefly differs in method, grouping SNPs into phaselets for hierarchical phasing with the cross-phaselet step targeted at quantum hardware.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
